{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966797,"nonce":"OIj7boIc2Tf+r8jbfjDNcaxqriE=","title":"Canvases nested inside an is_overlay_root subtree must dispatch AFTER","message":"Symptom: caret canvas inside a focused `cn::input` popover (or any canvas inside a portal / popover / dropdown / dialog / toast) is invisible. Reflows / scrolls / unrelated events don't restore it. Before the focused-bg fix it appeared to work because the host's unfocused bg matched the caret colour, but the caret was already being overpainted.\n\nMechanism. Frame paint order:\n1. Static cache blit.\n2. Canvas overlay (composite_frame canvas SDF pass) — every `CanvasPaintRecord` in the global pool.\n3. `dispatch_dynamic_batch_overlay` — popover / overlay-root bg \u0026 border SDF.\n4. Foreground overlay, motion text/svg, layer composites, images / meshes.\n\nWithout per-pool routing, a canvas in step 2 gets immediately overdrawn by step 3 when its host lives in an overlay-root subtree.\n\nFix. Canvases inherit an `in_overlay_subtree` flag from the walker and route into a sibling pool dispatched AFTER step 3.\n\nPieces:\n- `DrawContext::push_overlay_subtree` / `pop_overlay_subtree` / `in_overlay_subtree` — trait methods with no-op defaults. Required because inherent `GpuPaintContext` methods don't dispatch via `\u0026mut dyn DrawContext` (see [[gotcha-element-builder-trait-forwarding]] for the same shape).\n- `GpuPaintContext.overlay_subtree_depth: u32` — bracketed by trait-overridden push/pop AND by inherent push/pop forwarders.\n- Walker brackets `is_overlay_root` push/pop AROUND the existing `in_motion_subtree` push/pop (NOT inside it). Combined motion gate is not used; only the standalone `is_overlay_root` flag drives this counter.\n- `CanvasPaintRecord.in_overlay_subtree: bool` — set from `ctx.in_overlay_subtree()` at the canvas insert site.\n- `RenderTree.overlay_canvas_paint_records` — sibling pool to `canvas_paint_records`; cleared at full-paint start; insert routes by the flag.\n- `App::collect_overlay_canvas_overlay()` — sibling of `collect_canvas_overlay`. Both share the body via `collect_canvas_overlay_from(records, …)`.\n- `App::dispatch_overlay_canvas_overlay(view, \u0026overlay)` — sibling of `dispatch_dynamic_batch_overlay`. Calls `update_aux_data_slice(\u0026overlay.aux_data)`, `rebind_glyph_atlas_for_overlay()`, then `render_primitives_overlay(view, \u0026overlay.primitives)`. The aux re-upload is mandatory because `dispatch_dynamic_batch_overlay` just clobbered the GPU aux buffer with the dyn batch's data.\n- Three call sites: CSS fast path, binding fast path, slow path. Each runs `collect_overlay_canvas_overlay` alongside `collect_canvas_overlay`, then `dispatch_overlay_canvas_overlay` immediately after `dispatch_dynamic_batch_overlay`.\n\nWhen to extend. Any new class of primitives semantically above the overlay dyn-batch needs its own pass. Pattern is \"every new class of above-canvas primitives needs its own `render_primitives_overlay` pass\" from [[gotcha-overlay-canvas-z-interleave]] inverted for the nested case.\n\nWhat this does NOT fix:\n- Dynamic images / 3D meshes / GPU passes from canvases inside an overlay still ride the main canvas-overlay channel. The caret is a `fill_rect` so it's fine, but a canvas inside a popover that draws a video or an SVG icon will still z-fight the popover bg.\n- Fast-path `redraw_canvases` patches by record so it inherits the new flag transparently, but any new fast-path that bypasses records (none today) must respect the bucket.","files":null}]}